<title>CHINA: Pay differential widens for China graduates.</title>
<headline>Pay differential widens for China graduates.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>University graduates in China last year earned an average 70 percent more than employees with only primary level education, the Economic Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In 1990, graduates earned 20 percent more, the newspaper quoted the State Statistical Bureau as saying.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
